{title: Eye Of The Tiger}
{artist: Survivor}
{key: Am}

{c: Verse 1}
[Am] [F],        Risin up, back on the street,
[G] [Am],        Did my time, took my chances.
[Am] [F]
Went the distance, now Im back on my feet,
[G] [Am],        Just a man and his will to survive.
[Am] [F],        So many times, it happens too fast,
[G] [Am],        You change your passion for glory
[Am] [F]
Dont lose your grip on the dreams of the past,
[G] [Am],        You must fight just to keep them alive:
[G] [Am] [Dm],        Its the eye of the tiger,
[C] [G],        its the thrill of the fight
[Dm] [Am] [G]
Rising up to the challenge of our ri - val.
[Dm],        And the last known survivor
[C] [G],        stalks his prey in the night,
[Dm] [Em7] [F] [C] [Am]
& hes watchin us all with the eye of the tiger
[Am] [F],        Face to face, out in the heat,
[G] [Am],        Hangin tough, stayin hungry.
[Am] [F]
They stack the odds, still we take to the street,
[G] [Am],        For we kill with the skill to survive.
[G] [Am] [Dm],        Its the eye of the tiger,
[C] [G],        its the thrill of the fight
[Dm] [Am] [G]
Rising up to the challenge of our ri - val.
[Dm],        And the last known survivor stalks
[C] [G],        his prey in the night,
[Dm] [Em7] [F] [C] [Am]
& hes watchin us all with the eye of the tiger
[Am] [F],        Risin up, straight to the top,
[G] [Am],        Had the guts, got the glory.
[Am] [F],        Went the distance, now Im not gonna stop,
[G] [Am],        Just a man and his will to survive.
